{"id":"ce5a656462edb0c9","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-df-inner-product.md","title":"Inner Product","display":"df-inner-product — Inner Product","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-inner-product","aliases":["58-df-inner-product","Inner Product","Dot Product"],"display":"df-inner-product — Inner Product","depends_on":["[[58-df-vector-space]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-inner-product"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-inner-product</span><span>Inner Product</span><span>Dot Product</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-inner-product — Inner Product"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"592f9cfb66a507c2\" href=\"?note=592f9cfb66a507c2\" title=\"58-df-vector-space\">58-df-vector-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V,k,+_V,\\odot,B\\in V\\land k\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\">\\(V,k,+_V,\\odot,B\\in V\\land k\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{VectorSpace}_{(\\cdot)}(\\cdot,\\cdot,\\cdot):V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\operatorname{VectorSpace}_{(\\cdot)}(\\cdot,\\cdot,\\cdot):V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"592f9cfb66a507c2\" href=\"?note=592f9cfb66a507c2\" title=\"58-df-vector-space\">58-df-vector-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{InnerProduct}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{InnerProduct}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (本文件定义)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}inner\\text{-}product} \\vdash \\mathrm{InnerProduct}_S(B,V,k,+_V,\\odot)\\leftrightarrow k\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\land\\operatorname{VectorSpace}_k(V,+_V,\\odot)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(B,V\\times V,k)\\land\\forall x,y,z\\in V\\;\\forall\\alpha\\in k\\;\\left[\\begin{aligned}&amp;B\\!\\left(\\left\\langle +_V(\\langle x,y\\rangle),z\\right\\rangle\\right)=B(\\langle x,z\\rangle)+B(\\langle y,z\\rangle)\\\\&amp;\\land B\\!\\left(\\left\\langle\\odot(\\langle\\alpha,x\\rangle),y\\right\\rangle\\right)=\\alpha B(\\langle x,y\\rangle)\\\\&amp;\\land B(\\langle x,y\\rangle)=\\overline{B(\\langle y,x\\rangle)}\\land B(\\langle x,x\\rangle)\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\\\&amp;\\land\\Bigl(B(\\langle x,x\\rangle)=0\\leftrightarrow\\forall u\\in V\\;\\bigl(+_V(\\langle x,u\\rangle)=u\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\end{aligned}\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}inner\\text{-}product} \\vdash \\mathrm{InnerProduct}_S(B,V,k,+_V,\\odot)\\leftrightarrow k\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\land\\operatorname{VectorSpace}_k(V,+_V,\\odot)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(B,V\\times V,k)\\land\\forall x,y,z\\in V\\;\\forall\\alpha\\in k\\;\\left[\\begin{aligned}&amp;B\\!\\left(\\left\\langle +_V(\\langle x,y\\rangle),z\\right\\rangle\\right)=B(\\langle x,z\\rangle)+B(\\langle y,z\\rangle)\\\\&amp;\\land B\\!\\left(\\left\\langle\\odot(\\langle\\alpha,x\\rangle),y\\right\\rangle\\right)=\\alpha B(\\langle x,y\\rangle)\\\\&amp;\\land B(\\langle x,y\\rangle)=\\overline{B(\\langle y,x\\rangle)}\\land B(\\langle x,x\\rangle)\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\\\&amp;\\land\\Bigl(B(\\langle x,x\\rangle)=0\\leftrightarrow\\forall u\\in V\\;\\bigl(+_V(\\langle x,u\\rangle)=u\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\end{aligned}\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The function-graph convention is respected: the binary map <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B\">\\(B\\)</span> is applied to ordered pairs, as are <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"+_V\">\\(+_V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\odot\">\\(\\odot\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Inner product: positive definite sesquilinear form</li>\n<li>Cauchy-Schwarz: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|\\langle x, y \\rangle| \\leq \\|x\\| \\|y\\|\">\\(|\\langle x, y \\rangle| \\leq \\|x\\| \\|y\\|\\)</span></li>\n<li>Parallelogram: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|x+y\\|^2 + \\|x-y\\|^2 = 2\\|x\\|^2 + 2\\|y\\|^2\">\\(\\|x+y\\|^2 + \\|x-y\\|^2 = 2\\|x\\|^2 + 2\\|y\\|^2\\)</span></li>\n<li>Hilbert space: complete inner product space</li>\n<li>Orthogonal complement: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M^\\perp = \\{x : \\langle x, m \\rangle = 0 \\;\\forall m \\in M\\}\">\\(M^\\perp = \\{x : \\langle x, m \\rangle = 0 \\;\\forall m \\in M\\}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Rudin, Functional Analysis</li>\n<li>Reed and Simon, Functional Analysis</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-vector-space","status":"resolved","id":"592f9cfb66a507c2","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-vector-space]]","embed":false},{"target":".